// A stamp mill crushes ore under falling stamps. It stands against the gear at the foot of a shaft, driven by two
// counterweights on the same train (each blow lifts its stamps, about 1.8 kJ a lump: one 200 kg weight's 2 m fall
// crushes about two). Copper ore, iron ore and a stone dropped on its top go into its mortar and are broken one at a
// time: the ore into its concentrate and a lump of sand (the rock it was in), the stone into gravel, all out of the
// spout at its right foot. The weights share the work: the second drives the mill once the first is down.
map
##################################
##################################
#....jj*jjjjjjj*.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j.................#
#..........@...*.................#
##################################
##################################
end
give Counterweight 2
give StampMill 1
place 2 -7 -8 Counterweight          // a drum at the shaft's end...
place 2 -4 -7 Counterweight          // ...and one under the gear in its line
place 3 7 -1 StampMill
expect 4 works == 1
expect 4 weights == 2
drop 10 CopperOre 6 -7
drop 20 IronOre 6 -7
drop 30 Stone 6 -7
expect 60 stampload == 3             // in its mortar
expect 60 turning:5,0 == 1
expect 600 items:CopperFines == 1    // the first lump crushed...
expect 600 items:Sand == 1
expect 1200 stampload == 0           // ...and all three
expect 1200 items:IronFines == 1
expect 1200 items:Sand == 2
expect 1200 items:Gravel == 1
expect 1200 zone:CopperFines,8,14,-1,0 == 1    // out of the spout at its right foot
expect 1800 turning:5,0 == 0         // nothing left to crush: the weights hang still
